  "description": "NEKBAJ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H90 Gd5 N56 Ni10 O23 5+,5(N1 O3 1-),3(C2 H3 N1),5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 1 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 1 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 2 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 1 O neighbors; Ni5 (Ni) has 1 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3A (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Ni1A (Ni) has 1 O neighbors; Ni2A (Ni) has 1 O neighbors; Ni3A (Ni) has 2 O neighbors; Ni4A (Ni) has 1 O neighbors; Ni5A (Ni) has 1 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 22 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.612-4.008 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.66-128.85°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C86H103Gd5Ni10N64O43. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 5 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
